# ARK Earned Authority

**Full document:** [ark-earned-authority-v1.md](../../docs/ecosystem/ark-earned-authority-v1.md)

Governs **everything that leaves the shop** — not marketing only.

**Not Market Authority** (market trust / business health) — see [ark-market-authority.mdc](ark-market-authority.mdc).

Applies equally to: public website · Companion · advisor AI · voice AI · ARKademy · analytics · customer summaries · reports · social · email.

## Principle

**Authority is not created by publishing. Authority is earned through observation.**

> **Every public sentence should have a repair order standing behind it** — conceptually. If challenged: *"Here's why we know that."* Not: *"Every SEO guide says that."*

## Sources (only these create authority)

- Verified repair outcomes
- Repeated customer questions
- Documented diagnostic procedures
- Measured operational data
- Explicit shop policy

No inference, competitor mimicry, SEO templates, or AI fluency.

## Publication rule

Public knowledge is a **projection** of operational truth. Never invent, exaggerate, or infer beyond authority. **When uncertain, publish uncertainty.**

If evidence cannot be shown, do not present the claim as operational truth. See [ark-explainability-doctrine.mdc](ark-explainability-doctrine.mdc).

## Rejection test

Reject content that exists only for competitors, SEO, or assumption — especially fabricated confidence (invented repair counts, generic authority claims).

**Litmus:** If we deleted this sentence tomorrow, would any operational record miss it? If no — publication, not authority.

## Progression (gatekeeper)

```
Pressure → Observation → Vocabulary → Authority → Projection → Earned Authority
```

First five: how knowledge is created. Last: when it may leave the system.

## Public marketing v1 — closed (2026-07-06)

Foundation coherent. **Homepage layout frozen** until observation or analytics earns a change.

Public site evolves when **the shop earned something new to say** — not when someone has a new layout idea.

